\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  "Must I go, and empty handed"
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Thus my dear Redeemer meet?
\par Not one day or service give HIm.
\par Lay no trophy at His feet?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  "Must I go, and empty handed?
\par Must I meet my saviour so?
\par Not one soul with which to greet Him.
\par Must I empty handed go?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.   Not at death I shrink nor falter,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 For my Saviour saves me now;
\par But to meet Him empty-handed,
\par Though of that now clouds my brow.
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  "Must I go, and empty handed?
\par Must I meet my saviour so?
\par Not one soul with which to greet Him.
\par Must I empty handed go?
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. O the years in sinning wasted,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Could I but re-call them now,
\par I would give them to my Saviour,
\par to His will I'd gladlybow.
\par 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  "Must I go, and empty handed?
\par Must I meet my saviour so?
\par Not one soul with which to greet Him.
\par Must I empty handed go?
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  O ye saints, arouuse, be earnest,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Up and work while yet 'tis day;
\par Ere the night of death o'er take thee,
\par strive for souls while still you may
\par \pard 
